WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:04.200
-Guys, it's been an incredible,
incredible NFL playoff season,

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.667
and after yesterday's
crazy games,

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.567
we finally know who will be
in the Super Bowl.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.067
And, man,
it's going to be a good one.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.434
You've got two underdog teams --

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.534
the Cincinnati Bengals
taking on the Los Angeles Rams.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.901
You've got --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.434
You've got veteran quarterback
Matthew Stafford

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.267
going up against newcomer
Joe Burrow.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.601
I mean, it's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.667
It's nearly impossible to
predict who's going to win,

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.267
but you're in luck, because when
it comes to predicting things,

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.801
we have a secret weapon,
and it's puppies.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.601
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.400
Ladies and gentlemen,
it's time for the

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.567
"Puppy Predictors:
Super Bowl LVI Edition."

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.300
-♪ Puppy predictors ♪

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.400
♪ Puppy predictors ♪

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.300
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.100
We have one bowl of
delicious kibble

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.000
and two adorable puppies,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.133
one representing the Bengals,
the other representing the Rams.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.033
Whoever gets to the bowl first

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.767
will be crowned
Super Bowl champs.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:08.033
Now let's meet the puppies.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:13.367
♪♪

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.667
[ Audience "Awws" ]
Alright, guys.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.200
Yeah, nice to see you guys.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.934
Of course, we have --
hey, Ron --

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:26.267
we have Ron Bell
representing the Bengals.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:29.901
And representing the Rams,
we have Gary Frick Jr.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:30.934
Hey, Gary.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.934
Gary, how you doing, bud?

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:36.067
Nice to see you.
Oh, hi, guys. Hi, guys.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.167
That's right.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:39.634
Alright, now, guys,
before the show --

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.834
Before I release you here,
I want you to listen up.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.901
Gary, focus. Gary -- Yes.

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:46.000
Good boy. Wow. Look at him.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.667
Alright, now, I don't want any
wandering or butt sniffing.

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.100
I want this to be fair, okay?

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.801
Whoever gets to the -- Gary.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:56.634
Whoever gets to the bowl first
wins the Super Bowl.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.100
Yeah, that's right.
Look at the focus.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.934
Look at the focus.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.200
Look at the focus on these guys.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.634
That's the best
they've ever been.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.701
Alright, whenever we're ready.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.567
Release the puppies.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.934
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.167
Oh, my -- Wait. Who is it?
[ Dinging ]

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:23.767
We don't know. We don't know.
We have no idea.

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:27.133
We have to run the replay.
We have to -- There's a scandal.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:29.334
We have to run the replay.
It looks like...

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:34.601
Whoa! The winner of
the Super Bowl...

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:35.634
[ Dinging ]

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:38.467
...will be
the Cincinnati Bengals.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:44.501
Congratulations on the win, bud.
I'll put -- Thank you.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.067
[ Laughs ]

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:49.100
We'll be right back with
Peyton Manning, everybody.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.701
Congratulations to the Bengals.
Good job.

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:53.501
You did a good job.
You want to go back and eat?

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:56.968
♪♪

